{
  "title": "WHO Collective Action After Ostrom",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "[[Collective Action, Ostrom]] gives the Who shelf a structure the other shelves do not yet have. Thirty-one variables from decades of common-pool-resource research, and an ordered spine of three stages.",
      "id": "6fe039a65a88a787"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "10675e7a7ab35cbb",
      "text": "<svg style=\"width:100%;height:auto;display:block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 1053 818\"><rect width=\"1053\" height=\"818\" fill=\"#ffffff\"/>\n      <defs id=\"svg-defs\"><marker id=\"mk000000\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#000000\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkc53030\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#c53030\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkc05621\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#c05621\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkb7791f\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#b7791f\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk276749\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#276749\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk2b4c7e\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#2b4c7e\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk553c9a\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#553c9a\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk97266d\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#97266d\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk234e52\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#234e52\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk1a202c\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#1a202c\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk3b82f6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#3b82f6\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkf59e0b\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk8b5cf6\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk7c3aed\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/></marker><marker id=\"mkA83C2E\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#A83C2E\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk8A5F10\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#8A5F10\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk5A635E\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#5A635E\"/></marker><marker id=\"mk333333\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"10\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,1 L10,5 L0,9 Z\" fill=\"#333333\"/></marker></defs>\n      \n      <g id=\"wardley-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"lop-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"lines-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"edges-layer\"><g id=\"edge-h1\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 HEAVY in Marc's diagram. The first link of the highest-leverage chain in the model.</title><path d=\"M90,126 L90,214\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#A83C2E\" stroke-width=\"4.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mkA83C2E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"170\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-h2\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 HEAVY. Legal standing determines the strategy space a neighbourhood can see.</title><path d=\"M90,286 L90,374\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#A83C2E\" stroke-width=\"4.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mkA83C2E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"64\" cy=\"330\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-h3\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 And the perceived strategy space determines whether collective action forms at all. Three links, one claim: much of neighbourhood capacity is foreclosed upstream.</title><path d=\"M134.8479906814211,374 Q517.8,66.6 950,133.08004426410918\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#A83C2E\" stroke-width=\"4.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mkA83C2E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"526.1941984105312\" cy=\"130.3269303755588\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-h4\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 HEAVY. The second emphasised edge, and it lands on Survival rather than Performance.</title><path d=\"M786.8819875776397,360 Q868.2,481 950,493.36809176225233\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#A83C2E\" stroke-width=\"4.5\" marker-end=\"url(#mkA83C2E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"868.1873915735154\" cy=\"483.8417276553357\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-hb1\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Common Understanding feeds Trust.</title><path d=\"M401.08,193 Q382.6,235 404.16,284\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"363.0582091569253\" cy=\"231.58360299946244\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-hb2\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 And Trust feeds Common Understanding. The reinforcing pair at the centre of the model.</title><path d=\"M435.84,284 Q457.4,235 438.92,193\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"476.9417908430747\" cy=\"231.58360299946244\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-hb3\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Common Understanding makes conflict resolvable.</title><path d=\"M455.6808510638298,193 Q552.6,309.8 665,315.327868852459\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"552.3362484106395\" cy=\"311.69577441968056\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-hb4\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 And resolving conflict builds common understanding. A second reinforcing pair.</title><path d=\"M726.8085106382979,280 Q627.4,160.2 525,155.1639344262295\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"627.4338558902704\" cy=\"158.9011703198206\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-hb5\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 The hub reaches the outcomes through decision cost.</title><path d=\"M394.871875,193 Q326.5,310 398.9625,434\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"331.74558220788344\" cy=\"310.2607252345543\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-dc1\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Lower decision cost makes forming possible.</title><path d=\"M515,465.327868852459 Q810.4,450.8 1024.3191489361702,193\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"799.5576689813047\" cy=\"418.4287503249218\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-dc2\" style=\"cursor: grab; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 And keeps it working once formed.</title><path d=\"M515,489.1733181299886 Q770.8,540.8 1001.0075901328273,373\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" marker-end=\"url(#mk5A635E)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"767.8773311585348\" cy=\"515.7413388807059\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/></g><g id=\"edge-s1\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Ostrom's spine, stage one to two. You cannot manage what never properly formed.</title><path d=\"M1060,193 L1060,287\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"4\" marker-end=\"url(#mk333333)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"1034\" cy=\"240\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"then\" href=\"/then.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(90.0,1046.0,240.0)\"><tspan x=\"1046\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#333333\">then</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"edge-s2\" style=\"cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Stage two to three. Performing well is necessary and not sufficient — survival has its own drivers.</title><path d=\"M1060,373 L1060,467\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-width=\"4\" marker-end=\"url(#mk333333)\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"1034\" cy=\"420\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"then\" href=\"/then.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" pointer-events=\"none\" transform=\"rotate(90.0,1046.0,420.0)\"><tspan x=\"1046\" y=\"420\" font-size=\"10\" font-style=\"italic\" fill=\"#333333\">then</tspan></text></a></g></g>\n      <g id=\"nodes-layer\"><g id=\"node-gov\" transform=\"translate(90,90)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 External to the neighbourhood, and the origin of the heaviest chain in the model. Much local capacity is decided here before anyone local makes a choice.</title><rect x=\"-90\" y=\"-36\" width=\"180\" height=\"72\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"-32\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Governmental Agencies\" href=\"/governmental-agencies.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#171B19\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">Governmental Agencies</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-legal\" transform=\"translate(90,250)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 What government grants by way of legal standing and local prerogative. Drawn heavy by Marc on both sides — it receives one heavy edge and sends another.</title><rect x=\"-90\" y=\"-36\" width=\"180\" height=\"72\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"-32\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Legal Status, Local Prerogative\" href=\"/legal-status-local-prerogative.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#5E1F16\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">Legal Status, Local</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">Prerogative</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-alt\" transform=\"translate(90,410)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 The pivot. What a neighbourhood can even PERCEIVE as available to it. Foreclose this and the collective action never originates — no amount of local energy compensates.</title><rect x=\"-90\" y=\"-36\" width=\"180\" height=\"72\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"-32\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Perceived Alternative Strategies\" href=\"/perceived-alternative-strategies.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#5E1F16\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"-8.0\">Perceived Alternative</tspan><tspan x=\"0\" dy=\"16\">Strategies</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-hub\" transform=\"translate(420,150)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Highest-degree node in the full 31-variable model — seven in, three out. Nearly every RCN tool that produces a shared picture acts on this one variable, which was not designed.</title><polygon points=\"90.9,21.5 0.0,43.0 -90.9,21.5 -90.9,-21.5 -0.0,-43.0 90.9,-21.5\" fill=\"#FFF8E1\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"-39\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"COMMON UNDERSTANDING\" href=\"/common-understanding.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#4A3505\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">COMMON UNDERSTANDING</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-trust\" transform=\"translate(420,320)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Locked in a mutually reinforcing pair with Common Understanding — each feeds the other. Also fed by Similarities, Experience, Group Size and Distance to Resource.</title><polygon points=\"77.9,18.0 0.0,36.0 -77.9,18.0 -77.9,-18.0 -0.0,-36.0 77.9,-18.0\" fill=\"#FFF8E1\" stroke=\"#8A5F10\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><circle cx=\"86\" cy=\"-32\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"TRUST\" href=\"/trust.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#4A3505\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">TRUST</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-dcost\" transform=\"translate(420,470)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 The route by which Common Understanding reaches Origin and Performance. Shared understanding is not sentiment here — it is a cost reduction.</title><rect x=\"-95\" y=\"-36\" width=\"190\" height=\"72\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"91\" cy=\"-32\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Decision-making Costs\" href=\"/decision-making-costs.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#171B19\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">Decision-making Costs</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-conflict\" transform=\"translate(760,320)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Feeds Survival on the second heavy edge, and exchanges with Common Understanding in both directions. Groups do not usually die of poor execution; they die of unresolved conflict.</title><rect x=\"-95\" y=\"-40\" width=\"190\" height=\"80\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#5A635E\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"91\" cy=\"-36\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"Conflict Resolution\" href=\"/conflict-resolution.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#5E1F16\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">Conflict Resolution</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-origin\" transform=\"translate(1060,150)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Green — forming. Driven by Perceived Alternative Strategies, Decision-making Costs, Interdependence and subtractability, Asset Structure, Resource Scarcity. Reds concentrated here mean the collective action never properly originated, and no amount of management will help.</title><rect x=\"-110\" y=\"-43\" width=\"220\" height=\"86\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#E8F3EA\" stroke=\"#2F6B3C\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"-39\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"ORIGIN will it form?\" href=\"/origin-will-it-form.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#17401F\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">ORIGIN will it form?</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-perf\" transform=\"translate(1060,330)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Blue — managing. Driven by Enforcement Costs, Decision-making Costs, Dual Enforcement, Technology for Monitoring Resources, Speed of Access to Info. Reds here route to Sofi-VSM.</title><rect x=\"-110\" y=\"-43\" width=\"220\" height=\"86\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#E7F0F7\" stroke=\"#2C5F8A\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"-39\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"PERFORMANCE does it work?\" href=\"/performance-does-it-work.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#1B3B57\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">PERFORMANCE does it work?</tspan></text></a></g><g id=\"node-surv\" transform=\"translate(1060,510)\" style=\"cursor: move; opacity: 1;\"><title>📌 Red — surviving. Driven above all by Conflict Resolution, plus de facto vs de jure, Small Simple Set of Rules, Larger System of Institutional Support and Rate of Change. Reds here mean conflict work comes first and everything else second.</title><rect x=\"-110\" y=\"-43\" width=\"220\" height=\"86\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#F7E9E6\" stroke=\"#A83C2E\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"-39\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1\" pointer-events=\"none\"/><a class=\"internal\" data-title=\"SURVIVAL will it persist?\" href=\"/survival-will-it-persist.html\"><text text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"500\" fill=\"#5E1F16\" pointer-events=\"none\"><tspan x=\"0\" y=\"0.0\">SURVIVAL will it persist?</tspan></text></a></g></g>\n      <g id=\"triples-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"drag-layer\"/>\n      <g id=\"eip-statement-layer\"/>\n      \n      <g id=\"opm-symbols-chart\"/>\n    </svg>"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Three stages, in order",
      "id": "9d273c41432f4633"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "The top-level sequence is Origin, then Performance, then Survival. The colouring names what each stage is: green for forming, blue for managing, red for surviving. The Who question is not one question but three, asked in order.",
      "id": "4f157b8730e68e59"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "- Origin, forming. Will this collective action come into being at all? Driven by Perceived Alternative Strategies, Decision-making Costs, Interdependence and subtractability, Asset Structure, Resource Scarcity.\n- Performance, managing. Does it actually work once it exists? Driven by Enforcement Costs, Decision-making Costs, Dual Enforcement, Technology for Monitoring Resources, Speed of Access to Info.\n- Survival, surviving. Will it persist when conditions change? Driven above all by Conflict Resolution, plus de facto versus de jure, Small Simple Set of Rules, Larger System of Institutional Support, Rate of Change.",
      "id": "2de0c32308bce7cd"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Two chains are drawn heavy, and they are the leverage",
      "id": "63b232257a05dddb"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Governmental Agencies leads to Legal Status and Local Prerogative, which leads to Perceived Alternative Strategies, which leads to Origin.",
      "id": "b45b7cb665570b68"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "What government grants by way of legal standing and local prerogative determines which strategies a neighbourhood can even perceive as available. That determines whether the collective action originates at all.",
      "id": "604cbf4d5c3b23e5"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "This is the highest-leverage claim in the model, and it says something uncomfortable: a great deal of neighbourhood capacity is foreclosed upstream, before anyone in the neighbourhood makes a choice.",
      "id": "e637046756e602bb"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "The third heavy edge is Conflict Resolution to Survival. Not performance, not origin — survival. Groups do not usually die of poor execution; they die of unresolved conflict.",
      "id": "68285b4ebc3be5ed"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Common Understanding is the hub",
      "id": "0c242902afac0833"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Counting edges, Common Understanding is the highest-degree node in the model — seven in, three out — and it sits in a mutually reinforcing pair with Trust, each feeding the other. It also feeds Conflict Resolution, which feeds back into it.",
      "id": "291cf5fb36cc452c"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Nearly every RCN instrument that produces shared pictures — [[Campfire Conversations]], [[Cave Drawing]], the Graph Tool, MORE Outliner, FedWiki itself — is acting on the single most connected variable in Ostrom's model. The tools were not chosen with this model in mind, and they land on its hub anyway.",
      "id": "d725c905d364a4ec"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "It also means this model is exactly what a Vester run is for. Thirty-one variables with a dense feedback structure and no numbers is the Sensitivity Model's native input.",
      "id": "0dfdb50852981d7c"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "## Why three tools overlap on this shelf",
      "id": "cf40466050666f96"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Jon Walker correlated the VSM with Ostrom's work, and Marc correlated Sofi with the VSM. Ostrom, VSM and Sofi are in tight concordance, so Sofi-VSM on the Who shelf is not a competing framework — it is the same structure seen through an organizational lens. A neighbourhood can enter at whichever of the three is handiest, if they are made handy enough.",
      "id": "45073b97f023c359"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "text": "Applied to a real commons, this shelf becomes [[Collective Action Assessment]].",
      "id": "8912ca208077677c"
    }
  ],
